# FIXED DEFECT 426, found beside defect 411 by lane b13-w411 on 2026-10-06 and
# repaired there on 2026-10-07.
#
# SYMPTOM: `int32_t kr_write();`, a header declaration with no prototype, bound
# `kr_write(p: cstr lent)` and lent a `str` the program shared: exit 0, and C
# wrote it (`Zbc`). There was no parameter type to ask, and the call converted
# nothing.
#
# CAUSE: the pointee check reads such a function with no parameter, as it
# reads `int f(void)`, and asked nothing of it. FIX: a function the declaration
# gives a parameter, and the dump none, is asked whether its header gives a
# prototype at all (`emit/ffi_read_only.hero`), and one declared with none is
# refused on the declaration, naming the prototype a header of the author's
# own can give it.
#
# THIS SHAPE: a number. The definition takes a `double`, and a call with no
# prototype hands it an `int` unconverted, which C reads as a double.

extern "fixedbugs-426-no-prototype.h"
    function kr_double(n: i32) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(kr_double(n: 5))
